        {
          "id": "SP_MAZOCRAEOIDES_PRASHADI_CHAUHAN_1950",
          "name": "Mazocraeoides prashadi Chauhan, 1950",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Mazocraeoides",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Site in host: Gills. Specimens deposited: Zoological Survey of India, Kolkata, India. Voucher specimen 10436 / 1. Prevalence and mean intensity: 23.72 % and 1.5 worms per infected fish. Redescription: (Measurements based on 4 specimens) Body lanceolate, broad posteriorly, narrow anteriorly, tegument thick, opaque. Body size 1108 (976 – 1184) long, 304 (272 – 384) wide. Clamps four pairs, embedded in posterior half of body, with first pair at distance of 452 (416 – 528) from anterior end. All clamps of equal size, 20 x 21 long. Clamp skeleton with five sclerites, SAA, SAS, SMB, SMS, SL. Oral suckers oval, 25 (20 – 28) x 18 (16 – 20) in size. Pharynx elliptical, compact, muscular situated behind two anterior suckers. Esophagus long. Ceca broad with lateral branches extend to near posterior end of body. Lappet not differentiated from body proper. Posterior region of body provided with two pairs of anchors and one pair of hooks. Outer pair of anchors long, 10 in length, with straight shaft, prominent spur and curved blade. Inner pair of anchors smaller, 4.5 (4 – 5) long, hooks very small, visible only in few forms. Genital pore median, at distance of 170 (156 – 184) from anterior end. Testis single, oval, situated in intercecal region in posterior third of body.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:6480780"
        },
        {
          "id": "SP_MAZOCRAEOIDES_PURIENSIS_GUPTA_KRISHNA_1976",
          "name": "Mazocraeoides puriensis Gupta & Krishna, 1976",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Mazocraeoides",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "",
          "sourcedFrom": "none"
        },
        {
          "id": "SP_MAZOCRAEOIDES_ROTUNDUS_SAILAJA_SHAMEEM_MADHAVI_2019",
          "name": "Mazocraeoides rotundus Sailaja, Shameem & Madhavi, 2019",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Mazocraeoides",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "(Measurements based on 4 specimens) Body typically pot-like with broad rounded posterior region and narrow neck-like extensile anterior region. Some specimens appeared oval and plump probably due to contraction of anterior region. Body size small, 900 (832 – 976) long, 372 (336 – 432) wide. Clamps four pairs, of equal size, 23 (20 – 29) in diameter, sessile, closed type, embedded in body margins in posterior half of body, arranged equidistantly with first pair at distance of 520 (448 – 608) from anterior extremity, last pair close to posterior extremity. Clamp skeleton typical of Mazocraeoides comprises five sclerites: scleritum arcuatum-anterius (SAA), scleritum antero- supplementarium (SAS), scleritum medio-basale (SMB), scleritum medio-supplementarium (SMS) and scleritum labiatum (SL). Oral sucker oval, 26 (24 – 28) x 20 in size. Pharynx rounded, esophagus long, ceca broad, terminate at posterior region of body. Lappet not differentiated. Instead posterior region of body bears two pairs of anchors and one pair of hooks. Outer pair of anchors 43 (36 – 48) long, with broad shaft and prominent spur, curved tip. Inner pair of anchors smaller, 11 (8 – 12) long, hooks very small, visible only in some forms. Genital pore near intestinal bifurcation at distance of 143 (116 – 164) from anterior end. Testis single, oval, 150 (140 – 160) long, situated in intercecal field of posterior third of body. Seminal vesicle elliptical lies in front of testis.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:10143135"
        },
